# Project-specific agent context (private, and machine-generated in part).
# Two files because archeus writes the memory digest into whichever instructions
# file each installed CLI reads: CLAUDE.md for Claude Code, AGENTS.md for Codex
# and pi. They are the same artefact for different readers.
CLAUDE.md
# ANCHORED, unlike the line above, and the asymmetry is deliberate:
#   · `www/AGENTS.md` is written by `next dev` and is TRACKED — its own text
#     says to commit it — so a bare pattern here would shadow a real file.
#   · `core.ignorecase = true` on Windows, so a bare `AGENTS.md` would also
#     match `docs/agents.md`, which is a published page of the manual.
# `CLAUDE.md` stays unanchored because `www/CLAUDE.md` is archeus's too and is
# already ignored by it; anchoring that one would quietly un-ignore it.
/AGENTS.md

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.pyd

# Build artifacts (python -m build, and the venv the packaging check installs into)
build/
dist/
# `gem build` writes the packed pointer gem beside its gemspec
packaging/rubygems/*.gem
*.egg-info/
.wheeltest/
.ruff_cache/

# Windows
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Local setup / environment launchers (machine-specific)
Environment Start.bat
*.lnk
.claude/worktrees/

# Claude Code project agents (copied from the archeus library, machine-local)
.claude/agents/

# Workspace provenance manifest (machine-local: paths, session counts)
.archeus/

# Auto-generated per-module memory rules (regenerate on every memory refresh)
.claude/rules/archeus-mem-*.md

# The nudge hook's index — generated from .claude/agents/, which is itself
# machine-local, so committing the index would describe files that are not here
.claude/.archeus-agents.json

# Skills installed into this project from the bundled starters (machine-local,
# same as .claude/agents/ above)
.claude/skills/

# CLAUDE.md backups (machine-local)
CLAUDE.md.bak
claude-session-Fable-Claude-Script.md

# Design references + GUI screenshot output. Third-party stock/portfolio images
# we have no right to redistribute, and tools/shot_gui.py writes its captures
# here by default.
references/
# mkdocs build output
/site/

# scratch commit-message file
ARCHEUS_COMMITMSG

# ── transitional: the names this tool used before it was renamed ──────────
# Delete once every working copy has run the new version once (migrate.py moves
# these on first start). They are listed because until then they are UNIGNORED
# and stageable, and the contents are exactly what must never be committed:
# bash-log.txt is every command a session ran, injected-context.md is a whole
# transcript. The root .claudectl/ carries its own `.gitignore` holding `*`;
# these are the copies under subdirectories, which do not.
.claudectl/
.claude/rules/claudectl-mem-*.md
.claude/.claudectl-agents.json
CLAUDECTL_COMMITMSG

# Visual reference for the cluster language (notes/cluster-spec.md is measured
# out of these). ~11 MB of 3D models and 4K renders — kept on disk because the
# spec is only checkable against them, kept OUT of the repo because a design
# reference is not a build input and nobody cloning this needs eleven megabytes
# to run the tests.
notes/reference/

# iteration renders from the cluster/reference passes
.qa/
